#: sdlc/processes/publish-verification.bpmn:34
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run the verifier set (scripts/publish-verify.ts, `bun run cat publish:verify -- --dir <site>`) over the built tree. A SET: each verifier is one entry, and adding one changes nothing else. The first is JSON-LD expansion under a real processor, network refused — a property the context does not declare, a relative IRI or a context that will not load is a finding. Only documents of OURS are verified; third-party data in the tree is counted and cannot block."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/publish-verification.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run the verifier set over the built tree between the export and the deploy, and report pass, fail or could-not-tell. This process only verifies and says how it went. The caller (docs-site-publish) deploys either way, judges the outcome after the push, and routes anything but a pass through Process_PublishAlert, the one alert every failure shares."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/publish-verification.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs every verifier over the exported documents before anything is deployed, and reports pass, fail or could-not-tell. It decides nothing about the release: the caller blocks on anything but a pass."
msgstr ""

